{
  "_note": "Maps the 57 new cucumber models onto the 59 template names ServerScriptService.CucumberSpawner asks for in ServerStorage.Assets.BreakableModels. The spawner builds its lookup as Template = '<Zone> <Name>' from its RAW pools, so the grass biome's templates carry a 'Spawn ' prefix and three slots are served by a reused model.",

  "_quirks": {
    "Desert Desert Palm": "The spawner's RAW entry for the palm is {\"Desert Palm\", 2}, and it builds Template = zone .. ' ' .. name, so it asks for 'Desert Desert Palm'. The folder only ever had 'Desert Palm', so the palm has NEVER spawned - CucumberSpawner's own comment at line ~82 records that this once wedged DayNightCycle at PreparingDay until a missing-template guard was added. Providing both names fixes it with no code change.",
    "Desert Sliced Cucumber": "Desert's pool has BOTH 'Sun-Dried Slice' and a plain 'Sliced Cucumber'. The new set only has a desert sun-dried slice, so the plain one is served by the grass SlicedCucumber - which is what the name says it is.",
    "Cucumber Tree": "The spawner's generic TYPES pool (used by Toyland and Neon, which have no hand-modelled set) asks for a bare 'Cucumber Tree'. Served by the grass CucumberTree."
  },

